2. It does not speak for the upstream project
---------------------------------------------

This repository is a fork of DarkRTA/rb3, which carries no license. 629 commits
of this repository's history predate the fork point `a59c651b`, and changes
continue to be merged from upstream.

Those contributions belong to their authors, who have granted no license to
anyone. The CC0 in `LICENSE` applies, in its own words, only "to the extent
that [the Affirmer] is an owner of Copyright and Related Rights in the Work" —
so it waives this fork's contributors' rights and leaves upstream contributors'
rights untouched.

`doc/` is entirely upstream's. Every commit touching it is by Dark, Nathan or
rjkiv; this fork has contributed nothing to it. It holds reference material
rather than build inputs — `doc/src-old/` (1,727 files) and `doc/rb2_dump/`
(1,241 files) — and 911 of those files carry third-party licenses of their own,
described in section 3. Do not treat anything under `doc/` as CC0.

If you need clear rights to the upstream portion, ask upstream:
https://github.com/DarkRTA/rb3


