4. It makes no claim over the underlying game
----------------------------------------------

The sources under `src/`, excluding the third-party libraries in section 3, are
a decompilation of Rock Band 3, Build 100901_A, target `SZBE69_B8` — a work of
Harmonix Music Systems and MTV Games.

The CC0 waiver relinquishes this fork's contributors' interest in the
decompiled expression they wrote. It asserts nothing about, and grants nothing
in, the underlying game. Rights in the original work remain with their owners.

This repository contains no game assets, no game assembly, and no copyrighted
binaries. An existing, legitimately obtained copy of the game is required to
build it or do anything useful with it.


Reusing code from this repository
---------------------------------

Check which section a file falls under:

  scripts/, docs/
      Section 1. CC0, take it.

  native/
      Section 1, except native/include/httplib.h, which is MIT (section 3).

  tools/
      Mixed. Section 1 for this fork's contributions, section 2 for upstream's,
      and section 3 for tools/ninja_syntax.py (Apache 2.0).

  doc/
      None of it is ours. Section 2 for authorship, section 3 for the
      third-party source in doc/src-old/.

  src/system/{stlport,speex,zlib,synthwii/soundtouch},
  src/system/synth/tomcrypt, src/network/net/json-c, src/sdk/ec,
  src/sdk/PowerPC_EABI_Support/.../Math/Double_precision/
      Section 3. Third-party terms apply, including two copyleft libraries.

  Everything else under src/
      Section 1 for this fork's contributions, section 2 for upstream's, and
      section 4 for the underlying work.

